<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Workshops &mdash; Literary Science</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: 8rem 3rem 2.5rem;
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .page-header h1 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .page-header .page-desc {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--warm-gray); max-width: 500px;
  }

  .workshops-body {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 3rem 4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .workshops-body p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .workshops-body p strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .formats {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .format-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    transition: background 0.4s;
  }

  .format-row:hover { background: var(--paper-light); }

  .format-left {
    padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
  }

  .format-name {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .format-tag {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .format-right {
    padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .format-right p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 480px;
  }

  /* ── ENTRY POINTS ── */
  .entry-points {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }

  .entry-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 4rem 3rem 2rem;
  }

  .entry-header-label {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .entry-header h2 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.1rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .entry-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    transition: all 0.4s;
  }

  .entry-row:hover {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
  }

  .entry-row:hover .entry-num,
  .entry-row:hover .entry-desc { color: rgba(242,242,242,0.6); }

  .entry-num {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.45rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--faded);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    transition: color 0.4s;
  }

  .entry-content {}

  .entry-name {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .entry-desc {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    max-width: 480px;
    transition: color 0.4s;
  }

  /* contact strip */
  .contact-strip {
    padding: 5rem 3rem;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .contact-strip::before, .contact-strip::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute;
    top: 0; bottom: 0; width: 20px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,
      transparent 0px, transparent 3px,
      rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 3px, rgba(242,242,242,0.03) 4px);
  }
  .contact-strip::before { left: 0; }
  .contact-strip::after { right: 0; }

  .contact-strip h2 {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .contact-strip p {
    font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--paper-dark);
    max-width: 460px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .contact-strip a.contact-email {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 0.55rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-dark);
    padding: 0.7rem 1.6rem;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    transition: all 0.3s;
  }

  .contact-strip a.contact-email:hover {
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .entry-header,
    .entry-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .format-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .format-left { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-dark); padding: 1.5rem; }
    .format-right { padding: 1.5rem; }
    .workshops-body { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
    .entry-header { padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .entry-row { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <a href="/" class="nav-logo">Literary Science</a>
  <ul class="nav-links">
    <li><a href="/epistemology/">Methodology</a></li>
    <li><a href="/toolkit/">Toolkit</a></li>
    <li><a href="/studio/">Studio</a></li>
    <li><a href="/newcomm/">NewComm</a></li>
    <li><a href="/workshops/" class="active">Workshops</a></li>
    <li><a href="/about/">About</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<header class="page-header">
  <div class="section-label">Bring This to Your Space</div>
  <h1>Workshops</h1>
  <p class="page-desc">Literary Science runs in-person workshops for schools, museums, libraries, and community organizations.</p>
</header>

<div class="workshops-body reveal">
  <p>The methodology is open. The tools are free. You can read the epistemology, download the toolkit, and start practicing Literary Science in your own context tomorrow.</p>
  <p>Workshops are for institutions that want to go deeper. <strong>We come to your space</strong>, work with your people, and build capacity for your team to practice Literary Science on your own terms&mdash;with your own community, using your own texts.</p>
</div>

<div class="formats">
  <div class="format-row reveal">
    <div class="format-left">
      <div class="format-name">Half-Day Introduction</div>
      <div class="format-tag">3&ndash;4 Hours</div>
    </div>
    <div class="format-right">
      <p>The methodology in practice. Your team reads a text through the four movements, maps assets, traces flows, and begins building a hypothesis. You leave with a working understanding of how Literary Science operates.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="format-row reveal">
    <div class="format-left">
      <div class="format-name">Multi-Day Intensive</div>
      <div class="format-tag">2&ndash;5 Days</div>
    </div>
    <div class="format-right">
      <p>A full cycle. Your team works through every phase of the methodology using a novel and community data from your own context. By the end, you have a hypothesis document and the capacity to facilitate Literary Science independently.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="format-row reveal">
    <div class="format-left">
      <div class="format-name">Ongoing Partnership</div>
      <div class="format-tag">Semester or Year</div>
    </div>
    <div class="format-right">
      <p>We embed with your institution. Coaching, co-facilitation, and curriculum integration over a full term. For organizations ready to make Literary Science part of what they do&mdash;not a one-time event.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ── ENTRY POINTS ── -->
<div class="entry-points">
  <div class="entry-header reveal">
    <div class="entry-header-label">Entry Points</div>
    <h2>Where You Start Depends on Where You Stand</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-row reveal">
    <div class="entry-num">Pathway 01<br>Individual</div>
    <div class="entry-content">
      <div class="entry-name">Individual Educators</div>
      <p class="entry-desc">You teach a course and want to integrate the four movements into your existing practice&mdash;one classroom, one novel, one community connection at a time.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-row reveal">
    <div class="entry-num">Pathway 02<br>Department</div>
    <div class="entry-content">
      <div class="entry-name">English Departments</div>
      <p class="entry-desc">Your department wants to adopt Literary Science as a shared framework&mdash;aligning texts, assessments, and community engagement across multiple sections.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-row reveal">
    <div class="entry-num">Pathway 03<br>Institution</div>
    <div class="entry-content">
      <div class="entry-name">Schools &amp; Institutions</div>
      <p class="entry-desc">Your school is ready for cross-disciplinary integration&mdash;English, Math, and Literary Science working as a coordinated system with a shared community challenge.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="entry-row reveal">
    <div class="entry-num">Pathway 04<br>Partnership</div>
    <div class="entry-content">
      <div class="entry-name">Full Partnership</div>
      <p class="entry-desc">Your institution wants to become a site of community design&mdash;students leading real projects with real budgets, the campus transformed into shared infrastructure.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="contact-strip reveal">
  <h2>Let&rsquo;s talk.</h2>
  <p>Tell us about your space, your community, and what you&rsquo;re trying to build. We&rsquo;ll figure out what makes sense.</p>
  <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com" class="contact-email">hello@literaryscience.com</a>
</div>

<footer>
  <div class="footer-left">Literary Science</div>
  <div class="footer-right">A property of Asoluka LLC &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; <a href="mailto:hello@literaryscience.com">Contact</a> &nbsp;&mdash;&nbsp; &copy; 2026</div>
</footer>

<script>
  const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    entries.forEach(e => { if (e.isIntersecting) e.target.classList.add('visible'); });
  }, { threshold: 0.1 });
  document.querySelectorAll('.reveal').forEach(el => observer.observe(el));
</script>
</body>
</html>
